# Biology

MDCAT Biology follows the PMC/UHS 2025 syllabus, covering FSc Part I &amp; II topics (modern biology with molecular concepts). Top paid guides include **Dogar Brothers’ *National MDCAT Biology*** (latest edition) – about Rs. 1,258. Another popular choice is **WAK ETB Series: Biology for National MDCAT** (by Sajid Ali Khan, WAK Publishers, 1st Ed.) – sale price \~Rs. 1,140. Both align to the new syllabus and include extensive MCQs. *(Purchase via Daraz, Ilmi Book House, etc.)*

**Free/PDF:** The Punjab Board’s FSc Part-II Biology textbook (Biology Book–2) is freely available as a high-quality PDF, covering most syllabus topics. (Punjab Board FSc Part-I Biology PDFs are similarly available.) These official textbooks have comprehensive content and clear explanations, making them excellent free resources aligned to MDCAT topics.

# Chemistry

The MDCAT Chemistry syllabus spans FSc Part I &amp; II (organic, inorganic, physical chemistry). Key paid books include **Dogar Brothers’ *Smart Brain National MDCAT Chemistry Guide*** (latest ed.) – \~Rs. 1,100, and **WAK ETB Series: Chemistry for National MDCAT** – \~Rs. 2,000. These guides are updated for the PMC syllabus and contain detailed theory plus MCQs.

**Free/PDF:** The Punjab Board’s FSc Part-II Chemistry textbook PDF (Chemistry Book–2) is available online. This official text covers the exam topics thoroughly and can be downloaded for free (via Punjab Board or educational sites). Using it alongside problem sets ensures strong coverage of all chemistry concepts.

# Physics

Physics topics (mechanics, electricity, waves, modern physics) are drawn from FSc II. Recommended paid books include **Dogar Brothers’ *National MDCAT Physics (Smart Brain)*** – \~Rs. 770, and **WAK ETB Series: Physics for MDCAT** – \~Rs. 1,150. These are updated to the latest syllabus and provide thorough concept explanations with MCQs.

**Free/PDF:** The Punjab Board FSc Part-II Physics textbook (Physics Book–2) PDF is freely available. This official book has clear coverage of all required topics. Using the text (and its included worked examples) is a high-quality way to review physics fundamentals without cost.

# English

MDCAT English focuses on grammar, vocabulary, comprehension and précis. Useful paid resources include test-prep books by major publishers (e.g. KIPS or Ilmi Kitab Khana English prep guides). For example, the **WAK ETB Series: English for National MDCAT (1st Ed.)** has been listed (though it may be out of stock on Daraz). KIPS also offers “Entry Test English” prep books.

**Free/PDF:** The Punjab Board’s Class 12 English-II textbook *Modern Prose and Heroes* is available as a PDF and covers advanced grammar and vocabulary in context. While not specifically an MDCAT book, this official text helps build the language skills tested on the exam. (Similarly, English Grammar and Composition textbooks for 12th grade can be used as free resources.)

# Logical Reasoning

Logical Reasoning is typically practiced via question banks and past papers. Paid options include **Dogar’s MDCAT MCQs guide by Dr. Afzaal Bajwa (25,000+ MCQs)** – a comprehensive collection covering logic puzzles and reasoning (≈Rs. 2,499). Other publishers like KIPS offer separate logical reasoning practice books.

**Free/PDF:** No official free “logic” textbook exists, but students often use past MDCAT papers (published by PMC/UHS) and free online reasoning question compilations to practice. For example, the MDCAT past-paper PDFs (available on PMC/UHS or educational portals) include the logic sections and can be downloaded at no cost.

**Sources:** Official exam syllabus and prep guides; Daraz and publisher listings for book details and prices. (Free PDFs cited from Punjab Board textbooks.)</pre>
